WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.721
arrived at the door of Mayor Madeleine's factory and was promptly hired.

2
00:00:21.441 --> 00:00:24.862
She had no experience in making jewelry, so she worked slowly.

3
00:00:25.723 --> 00:00:30.304
As a result, she did not receive much money for each day's work, but it was enough.

4
00:00:31.176 --> 00:00:34.278
Fantine thought only of Cosette and their future together.

5
00:00:34.918 --> 00:00:39.340
Because Fantine wasn't married, she was careful never to mention her little girl to anyone.

6
00:00:40.081 --> 00:00:43.683
She rented a small room and borrowed money to buy furniture for it.

7
00:00:44.483 --> 00:00:48.105
Fantine was earning her own living, and she was almost happy.

8
00:00:49.006 --> 00:00:53.328
Meanwhile, thanks to Fantine, Monsieur Thenardier had been able to pay his debt.

9
00:00:54.048 --> 00:01:00.232
Within a month the family needed more money, so Madame Thenardier took Cosette's clothes to Paris, where she

10
00:01:00.332 --> 00:01:00.852
sold them.

11
00:01:01.736 --> 00:01:05.317
When this money ran out, the Thenardiers began to resent Cosette.

12
00:01:05.997 --> 00:01:08.378
They dressed her in rags and fed her leftovers.

13
00:01:09.179 --> 00:01:11.679
She ate under the table with the dog and the cat.

14
00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:17.781
Since Fantine could not read or write, she hired a man to write her letters for her.

15
00:01:18.682 --> 00:01:20.742
She wrote twice a month to the Thenardiers.

16
00:01:21.823 --> 00:01:25.724
Their reply was always the same: Cosette is doing wonderfully well.

17
00:01:26.608 --> 00:01:31.713
After a year Monsieur Thenardier demanded that Fantine pay 12 francs a month instead of 7.

18
00:01:32.393 --> 00:01:36.897
Fantine gladly sent the money because she thought Cosette was being well cared for.

19
00:01:37.738 --> 00:01:44.123
In reality Madame Thenardier loved her own daughters, Eponine and Azelma, and hated Cosette.

20
00:01:45.384 --> 00:01:49.407
Seeing their mother treating Cosette cruelly, the two girls did the same.

21
00:01:50.188 --> 00:01:54.492
Meanwhile people in Fantine's hometown watched her and gossiped about her.

22
00:01:55.152 --> 00:01:59.635
More than one person was envious of her thick blond hair and fine white teeth.

23
00:02:00.435 --> 00:02:04.698
It became common knowledge that she wrote regularly to the innkeeper in Montfermeil.

24
00:02:05.418 --> 00:02:09.821
The man who wrote her letters could not keep a secret; he was the one who revealed that

25
00:02:09.861 --> 00:02:10.761
she had a child.

26
00:02:12.222 --> 00:02:16.264
An old woman who liked to gossip wanted to find out for herself what was going on.

27
00:02:17.025 --> 00:02:22.108
She traveled to Montfermeil, talked to the Thenardiers, and actually saw Cosette.

28
00:02:23.016 --> 00:02:27.240
Monsieur Thenardier decided to demand 15 francs a month from Fantine.

29
00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:30.702
Somehow the young woman managed to make the payments.

30
00:02:31.443 --> 00:02:37.208
But soon after the old woman returned from Montfermeil, Fantine was summoned by the factory supervisor.

31
00:02:38.028 --> 00:02:43.292
This supervisor told Fantine that she was no longer employed and handed her fifty francs.

32
00:02:44.013 --> 00:02:48.216
The supervisor also told her that the mayor had suggested that she leave the city.

33
00:02:48.937 --> 00:02:50.038
Fantine was shocked.

34
00:02:50.058 --> 00:02:52.540
"I cannot leave the city," she thought.

35
00:02:53.052 --> 00:02:55.735
"I am in debt for my rent and my furniture."

36
00:02:56.575 --> 00:03:00.399
Fifty francs wasn't enough to pay her debts, never mind transportation.

37
00:03:01.059 --> 00:03:04.342
Ashamed and distraught, Fantine slipped away to her room.

38
00:03:05.103 --> 00:03:10.207
After that, it did not take long for Fantine to fall behind on her payments to the Thenardiers.

39
00:03:11.928 --> 00:03:13.370
Two more years passed.

40
00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:19.215
If Fantine had been able to return to Montfermeil, she would not have recognized her child.

41
00:03:20.748 --> 00:03:25.150
Cosette, so fresh and pretty when she'd arrived at the inn, was now thin and pale.

42
00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:27.231
Cruelty had made her ugly.

43
00:03:28.051 --> 00:03:30.512
Her large blue eyes were filled with sadness.

44
00:03:31.252 --> 00:03:35.774
She was a miserable sight to see in the winter, sweeping the sidewalk before daybreak.

45
00:03:36.614 --> 00:03:40.596
Everyone called her the Lark because she was like a tiny, busy bird.

46
00:03:41.256 --> 00:03:43.237
Only this poor lark never sang.

47
00:03:44.117 --> 00:03:45.658
What had become of Fantine?

48
00:03:46.238 --> 00:03:50.300
When she was fired from the factory, she thought that she would get a job as a servant.

49
00:03:50.996 --> 00:03:54.079
She went from one house to another, but nobody wanted her.

50
00:03:54.859 --> 00:03:59.463
The furniture dealer to whom she owed money said, "If you leave the city, I'll have you arrested

51
00:03:59.523 --> 00:04:00.044
as a thief!"

52
00:04:00.845 --> 00:04:02.466
Her landlord also threatened her.

53
00:04:03.106 --> 00:04:07.470
So Fantine divided the little money she had between the furniture dealer and the landlord.

54
00:04:09.132 --> 00:04:10.453
It still was not enough.

55
00:04:11.093 --> 00:04:14.176
She began to make shirts for the soldiers at the local garrison.

56
00:04:14.936 --> 00:04:19.304
She earned 12 sous a day; Cosette was costing her 10 sous.

57
00:04:19.324 --> 00:04:23.505
She lived as cheaply as she could, doing without heat or even a candle.

58
00:04:24.285 --> 00:04:26.346
Her clothes became more and more ragged.

59
00:04:27.226 --> 00:04:30.227
Fantine had one friend: her neighbor Marguerite.

60
00:04:30.247 --> 00:04:35.209
"If I sleep only five hours a night and work the rest of the time, I might have

61
00:04:35.229 --> 00:04:37.049
enough money," she told Marguerite.

62
00:04:37.769 --> 00:04:40.050
But over time Fantine became exhausted.

63
00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:42.571
The slight cough she had grew worse.

64
00:04:43.171 --> 00:04:47.292
Sometimes she said to Marguerite, "Just feel how hot my hands are."

65
00:04:48.068 --> 00:04:52.771
One day the Thenardiers wrote to Fantine and said that Cosette didn't have any winter clothes.

66
00:04:53.492 --> 00:04:56.974
They said that Fantine must send at least ten francs for a wool skirt.

67
00:04:57.655 --> 00:04:59.696
All day Fantine worried about what to do.

68
00:05:00.256 --> 00:05:02.098
That evening she went to the barbershop.

69
00:05:03.599 --> 00:05:04.940
"What beautiful hair!"

70
00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:08.262
said the barber when Fantine removed the combs from her head.

71
00:05:08.902 --> 00:05:10.623
Her hair hung down to her waist.

72
00:05:10.644 --> 00:05:12.685
"How much will you give me for it?

73
00:05:13.225 --> 00:05:15.467
I understand there's a demand for hair for wigs."

74
00:05:15.487 --> 00:05:16.888
"Ten francs."

75
00:05:17.592 --> 00:05:20.874
"Then cut it all off," she said quickly before she could change her mind.

76
00:05:21.614 --> 00:05:24.576
Fantine bought a knit skirt and sent it to the Thenardiers.

77
00:05:25.316 --> 00:05:26.377
They were furious.

78
00:05:27.137 --> 00:05:30.939
They had wanted the money, not the skirt, so they gave the skirt to Eponine.

79
00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:34.341
Cosette still shivered, but Fantine was happy.

80
00:05:34.361 --> 00:05:37.943
"My child is no longer cold," she told Marguerite.

81
00:05:38.484 --> 00:05:40.045
"I have clothed her with my hair."

82
00:05:40.685 --> 00:05:41.886
She didn't know the truth.

83
00:05:42.706 --> 00:05:47.893
Fantine put on a little round cap to conceal her short hair and somehow still managed to look

84
00:05:47.933 --> 00:05:51.734
pretty. But she felt sad that she had had to cut her beautiful hair.

85
00:05:53.354 --> 00:05:58.355
Every time she passed the factory, she resented Mayor Madeleine and blamed him for her troubles.

86
00:05:59.236 --> 00:06:01.696
Soon she received another letter from the Thenardiers.

87
00:06:02.337 --> 00:06:06.358
Cosette was seriously ill with a fever and her medicine was expensive.

88
00:06:06.378 --> 00:06:12.699
"Unless you send us forty francs," wrote Monsieur Thenardier, "your daughter will surely die."

89
00:06:12.719 --> 00:06:14.440
"Forty francs!

90
00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:16.801
Where will I get that kind of money?"

91
00:06:17.281 --> 00:06:18.462
Fantine asked Marguerite.

92
00:06:19.223 --> 00:06:24.706
But that very day, she noticed a traveling dentist in the square, and he noticed her beautiful white

93
00:06:24.786 --> 00:06:30.230
teeth. "If you will sell me two of your front teeth," said the dentist, "I'll pay you well.

94
00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:33.172
Your teeth will make wonderful false teeth."

95
00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:34.873
"Don't be ridiculous!"

96
00:06:35.273 --> 00:06:36.014
said Fantine.

97
00:06:36.034 --> 00:06:37.955
"How much money did he offer?"

98
00:06:38.376 --> 00:06:40.657
asked Marguerite, when Fantine told her the story.

99
00:06:40.677 --> 00:06:42.678
"Twenty francs per tooth."

100
00:06:43.259 --> 00:06:45.812
"That's forty francs," said Marguerite.

101
00:06:45.832 --> 00:06:49.653
"I know," said Fantine quietly.

102
00:06:49.673 --> 00:06:52.314
"Have you ever heard of this kind of fever?"

103
00:06:52.694 --> 00:06:54.795
She showed the Thenardiers' letter to Marguerite.

104
00:06:55.295 --> 00:06:56.715
"Does it attack children?

105
00:06:56.735 --> 00:06:58.796
Do people really die from it?"

106
00:06:58.816 --> 00:07:03.497
"Yes, people die, especially children," said Marguerite.

107
00:07:04.237 --> 00:07:06.758
Later that night Fantine went in search of the dentist.

108
00:07:07.458 --> 00:07:10.159
She sent the forty francs to the Thenardiers right away.

109
00:07:10.819 --> 00:07:11.699
Poor Fantine!

110
00:07:12.379 --> 00:07:14.760
She didn't know that Cosette wasn't really sick.

111
00:07:15.304 --> 00:07:18.166
It was all a trick for the Thenardiers to get more money from her.

112
00:07:18.927 --> 00:07:21.609
Fantine coughed while she sewed the soldiers' shirts.

113
00:07:22.249 --> 00:07:25.111
She was coughing when she read Monsieur Thenardier's next letter.

114
00:07:25.131 --> 00:07:28.094
"Cosette is still recovering," he wrote.

115
00:07:28.114 --> 00:07:32.517
"I must have one hundred francs immediately or I will have to turn her out into the street."

116
00:07:33.858 --> 00:07:34.719
"What will I do?"

117
00:07:34.739 --> 00:07:34.839
cried
